A couple of tips to avoid this in the future:

Commit working versions to Git frequently so you can easily compare or restore deleted files.
If something suddenly stops working, git status and git diff are often the fastest way to spot accidental deletions or changes.
For Express apps serving static files, it's also handy to verify that publicFolder/index.html exists whenever GET / starts returning Cannot GET /.

